      "id": 1,
      "text": "Davidsville was laid out in 1831 by David Stutzman, surveyed by Thomas Gaghegan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Davidsville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first house appeared same year, built by Joseph Schell & Peter Levy; a blacksmith shop followed in 1832, and a schoolhouse emerged around 1835.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Davidsville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A Lutheran church was erected in 1852, marking the town's early religious life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Davidsville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Conemaugh Historical Society at 104 North Main Street preserves local history and offers research appointments.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
